/**
 * A dynamic axis out of range is an error about the pass's own parameter, not about a node of the
 * program: the pass reports it when it translates the program. The case used to name the exported
 * function in an export_model call; the thin stage form translates the program the command line
 * hands it. The program has one tensor input, whose rank the axis is
 * checked against -- without an input the check has no rank to look at, which is why this case
 * could pass or fail before for a reason that had nothing to do with the axis.
 */

func main(x: f32[2]) => f32[2] sync {
    return x
}